--
N5008 [expr.ass]/8.1: `x = B' with a braced-init-list B and a scalar x means
`x = t' where `T t = B'; [dcl.init.list]/3.11: an empty list
value-initializes, i.e. zero-initializes a scalar ([dcl.init.general]/9).
The C++ front end rejected the assignment for an enumeration type ("invalid
implicit conversion from '<<type:>>' to 'enum errc'"); libstdc++'s <charconv>
writes `__res.ec = {};' in __to_chars_10/16/8/2 and __to_chars, so
std::to_chars for every integer type was dropped (round 162 audit).  Fixed in
round 163: implicit_typecast value-initializes a scalar target from `{}'.
